  "interpretation": [
    "The alpha=.05 amplitude lower bound uses unqualified saved force estimates and is not an independent physical prediction.",
    "Density remainder and coefficient tails must be assessed after subtracting rigid completion components; q magnitude alone is not a mesh criterion.",
    "Full17 resistance conditioning is distinct from the BIE operator conditioning; the former was measured previously, the latter has not been estimated here.",
    "At fixed beta, alpha changes a lower-order single-layer term. It cannot be assumed to remove physical close-gap gradients or all high-frequency density structure."
  ],
  "proposed_controlled_diagnostic_not_executed": [
    "After the active solve, first test D-only exterior traces of each body rigid mode at existing independent surface sites. This checks whether small-alpha completion amplification would amplify quadrature errors.",
    "On one modest same-pose/h150 mesh assemble S and D separately once; compare alpha=.05,.2,1 with beta1 for relative-normal approach and one worst torque/strain mode. These are representation screening only, not qualification sources.",
    "Record scaled original-operator linear residual, condition estimate or GMRES convergence, rigid-subtracted density tails, all-surface plus gap boundary max/RMS on an independent denser site set, and physical F/T/S.",
    "A promising coefficient must preserve F/T/S within independently established uncertainty and improve independent boundary checks under refinement. Freeze it before a new same-source three-mesh sequence and isolated moment validation."
  ],
